{"created": "2025-08-11T23:31:57.797227+00:00", "modified": "2025-08-11T23:32:00.134759+00:00", "id": 16790538, "conceptrecid": "16790537", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.16790538", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.16790537", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.16790538", "metadata": {"title": "FlareDB: A Database of Significant Flares in Solar Cycles 24 and 25 with SDO/HMI and SDO/AIA Observations - Quick-look Movies", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.16790538", "publication_date": "2025-08-10", "description": "<p>Quick-look movies from the FlareDB database of of Significant Flares in Solar Cycles 24 and 25 with SDO/HMI and SDO/AIA Observations. Each compressed (.zip) file contains 151 moives, corresponding to 151 significant flare events.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>FlareDB_event_list.pdf: <br></strong>This file lists the events, including the soft X-ray class, NOAA active region number, flare start, peak, and end times, and the HMI Active Region Patches (HARP) number.</li>\n<li><strong>FlareDB_data_structure.jpg: <br></strong>This figure shows the structure of the FlareDB, indicating the type of data contained in each ZIP file.</li>\n<li><strong>HPC/CEA:&nbsp;<br></strong>Helioprojective Cartesian Coordinates / Lambert Cylindrical Equal-Area projections</li>\n<li><strong>12m:</strong> <br>AIA data with a 12-minute cadence, covering 32 hours, matching the HMI data.</li>\n<li><strong>12s/24s:</strong> <br>AIA data with a 12-second cadence for EUV wavelengths and a 24-second cadence for UV wavelengths, covering only the flare period.</li>\n<li><strong>94A/131A/171A/193A/211A/304/335A:</strong><br>Extreme Ultraviolet (EUV) wavelengths in units of &Aring;ngstr&ouml;m.</li>\n<li><strong>1600A/1700A:</strong><br>Ultraviolet (EUV) wavelengths in units of &Aring;ngstr&ouml;m.</li>\n<li><strong>Magnetogram:</strong><br>Line-of-sight (LOS) magnetogram.</li>\n<li><strong>Bz/Bt:</strong><br>Vertical (z-component) and transverse (x- and y-component) magnetic fields.</li>\n<li><strong>continuum:</strong><br>&nbsp;Pseudo-continuum intensity.</li>\n</ul>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Liu, Nian", "affiliation": "New Jersey Institute of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0002-6018-3799"}, {"name": "Abduallah, Yasser", "affiliation": "New Jersey Institute of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0003-0792-2270"}, {"name": "Kapure, Tanmay", "affiliation": "New Jersey Institute of Technology"}, {"name": "Li, Qin", "affiliation": "New Jersey Institute of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0002-3669-1830"}, {"name": "Wang, Haimin", "affiliation": "New Jersey Institute of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0002-5233-565X"}, {"name": "Wang, Jason", "affiliation": "New Jersey Institute of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0002-2486-1097"}], "contributors": [{"name": "Liu, Yang", "affiliation": null, "type": "DataCurator", "orcid": "0000-0002-0671-689X"}, {"name": "Zhang, Rui", "affiliation": null, "type": "DataCurator"}], "dates": [{"type": "updated"}], "version": "2025-05-31", "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/Reasopprime/njit-flaredb", "code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}}]}, "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "16790537"}}]}}, "title": "FlareDB: A Database of Significant Flares in Solar Cycles 24 and 25 with SDO/HMI and SDO/AIA Observations - Quick-look Movies", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/16790538", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/16790538", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/16790538?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.16790538", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.16790538", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.16790538", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/16790538/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/16790537", "parent_html": "https://zenodo